# Two impls on DIFFERENT types, in different files, each declaring `label` — a
# shape `L0398` permits (it only keeps free-function and trait-method namespaces
# disjoint). Both bodies sit at the same `(line, column)`, and a `Span` carries
# no file, so `a.lby`'s scalar `pik(self.v)` and `b.lby`'s heap
# `len(to_string(self.v))` collide in the checker's expression-type table.
#
# Keying that table on `(function name, span)` made the first match win: the gate
# read `Card::label`'s `i64`, concluded there was no heap value, descended past
# `Coin::label`'s `to_string`, and let a real heap string be built inside a
# `--freestanding` no-CRT binary (observed: `check` exit 0, native binary exit 9).
# The key must carry the origin module too.
no-runtime
import a
import b

fn main -> i64
    let c Card = Card(3)
    let k Coin = Coin(123456)
    c.label() + k.label()
